{
 "about": "Scribble-to-erase (docs/dev/handwriting.md 'What the user sees' and 'Client': frontend/src/ink/gestures.js isScribble and scribbleTargets). `samples` are one finished pen stroke in page points at scale 1, each [x, y, p, t] (x, y in pt to 0.01, p 0..1, t integer ms since the first sample); `k` is css px per pt. `scribble` is what isScribble(samples as {x, y, p, t}, {k}) must return (the duration is the samples' own: last t minus first). A case with `groups` also pins scribbleTargets(samples, groups, {keep}): `groups` are the page's ink groups in order, each {gid, strokes: [{id, tool, brush?, size, samples: [[x, y], ...]}]} (the test builds each stroke with encodeStroke, channels xy, colour #1f1f1f, and the group as {id: gid, ink: {strokes}}); `filter` is the eraser filter the keep function is built from (ink.js eraserKeep: 'all' keeps every stroke, 'pen' tool pen of any brush, 'highlighter' tool highlighter; an unknown tool only under 'all'); `targets` is the exact answer, [{gid, ids}] in group order with ids in file order, groups with no target left out. A stroke is a target when its bounding box lies at least 70 % (by area) inside the scribble's bounding box, it is not a highlighter, its box is not more than 3x the scribble's (by diagonal) and keep accepts it. frontend/tests/gestures.test.mjs reads this; backend/tests/test_shared_fixtures.py only checks each case's shape.",
